    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0805" n="785" xml:id="pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/9–2650: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Korea
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-09-26T19:00:00-05:00">September 26,
                            1950—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>151. Although Dept appreciates difficulties involved, in view apparent
                    possibility imminent return of ROK Govt to Seoul request you make every effort
                    discourage Rhee or other ROK spokesmen making pronouncements re ROK’s unilateral
                    extension authority north 38°. This matter being considered highest Govt levels;
                    also of vital concern to all UN member states. Any unilateral public statement
                    from ROK can only have harmful effect on attitude UN members. ROK delegation in
                    confidential discussions with other UN delegations is at this time most
                    effective method conveying ROK views. You shld emphasize to Rhee his cooperation
                    with UN at this time of utmost importance to future ROK.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
